Technical Specification: Spaceware – Proxima Descent (Version 4.2)
Inventory & Crafting System – Active Resource Management

• 1. Prerequisites

V4.1 must be fully functional before implementing V4.2:
- Joystick visible and responsive in both spaceship and astronaut modes.
- Game phase switches correctly between DESCENT, LANDING_CUTSCENE, and SURFACE_EXPLORATION.
- Buttons S, J, A, I visible and responsive in SURFACE_EXPLORATION mode.

• 2. Button S – Scan (Active Resource Discovery)

Function: Detects buried resources within a short radius of the astronaut.

When activated:
- Temporary icons for Scrap, Food, or Artifacts appear at random locations near the astronaut.
- Icons remain visible for 5 seconds, then fade out if not collected.

Cooldown: 15 seconds. Cannot scan while cooldown is active.
Scan does not consume any resources.

Implementation:
-----------------------------
| if (scanCooldown <= 0) {  |
| revealResources(radius=100);|
| scanCooldown = 15;        |
| }                         |
-----------------------------

• 3. Button J – Jump (Mobility)

Function: Allows the astronaut to clear small terrain depressions or reach elevated resources.

Effect: Brief Y-axis displacement (upward then downward). Total duration 0.5 seconds.
Cooldown: 2 seconds (prevents spam, not a power-up).
Camera does not change during jump.

Without jump, movement is limited to flat lateral sliding (joystick only).

• 4. Button A – Attack (Defense)

Function: Fires a plasma projectile (simple SVG) that destroys small obstacles or enemies (when implemented).

Projectile behavior:
- Moves horizontally in a straight line from astronaut's position.
- Instant damage at impact point.
- Destroys on collision with any obstacle or enemy.
- If no collision, projectile disappears after traveling 500 pixels.

Cooldown: 3 seconds. Unlimited ammunition.

• 5. Button I – Inventory (Resource Management)

Function: Opens a modal window (no game reload, no screen freeze) showing two panels:

• 5.1 Available Materials
- Scrap: [current count]
- Food: [current count]
- Artifacts: [current count]
- All counts update in real time as resources are collected.

• 5.2 Crafting Recipes

List of upgrades the player can craft if they have the required materials.

Example Recipes (expandable):

| Upgrade | Cost | Benefit |
|---------|------|---------|
| Enhanced Engine | 20 Scrap + 5 Artifacts | +10% movement speed (permanent) |
| Hydroponic Farm | 15 Scrap + 10 Food | Generates 1 Food every 30 seconds (passive) |
| Energy Shield | 30 Scrap + 15 Artifacts | Absorbs 1 hit (permanent, one-time shield) |
| Scanner Booster | 25 Scrap + 8 Artifacts | Reduces Scan cooldown from 15s to 10s |
| Jump Pack | 12 Scrap + 6 Food | Double jump height (permanent) |

• 5.3 Crafting Rules

- If the player has enough materials, the "Craft" button is enabled.
- When crafted:
  - Materials are deducted from inventory.
  - Upgrade effect is applied immediately.
  - Recipe remains visible but becomes uncraftable if materials are insufficient.
- Upgrades are permanent for the current session. No reset on game over.

Implementation:
-----------------------------
| if (scrapCount >= costScrap && artifactsCount >= costArtifacts) { |
|   scrapCount -= costScrap;                                       |
|   artifactsCount -= costArtifacts;                               |
|   applyUpgradeEffect(upgradeId);                                 |
| }                                                               |
-----------------------------

• 6. Inventory Modal Behavior

- Opens with button I, closes with X button or by tapping outside the modal.
- Game does not pause while modal is open (resources continue to spawn, oxygen depletes if implemented).
- Player can close modal, collect more resources, and reopen to craft additional upgrades.
- Modal state (scroll position, selected recipe) does not need to persist after closing.

• 7. Resource Integration

- Resources (Scrap, Food, Artifacts) already spawn passively from V3.
- Scan adds active discovery (more resources, higher density).
- All resource counts are shared between main HUD and inventory modal.
- Collecting a resource updates both displays in real time.

• 8. Crafting Effects (Permanent)

| Effect | Implementation |
|--------|----------------|
| Movement speed | Multiply joystick speed by 1.1 |
| Passive Food generation | Add 1 Food every 30 seconds via timer |
| Energy Shield | Set shielded=true; first hit does no damage, then shield breaks |
| Scanner Booster | Reduce scanCooldown max from 15 to 10 |
| Double jump | Add second jump while airborne (cooldown resets on ground) |

• 9. Integration with Game Phases

| Version | Phase | Features |
|---------|-------|----------|
| V1 | Descent | Joystick only |
| V2 | Landing cutscene | No controls (cinematic) |
| V3 | Surface exploration | Passive resource spawn |
| V4.1 | Surface exploration | Joystick + buttons S/J/A/I visible and responsive |
| V4.2 | Surface exploration | V4.1 + Scan, Jump, Attack, Inventory, Crafting (this version) |

• 10. Deliverable

A functional Rezona game that includes ALL previous versions (V1, V2, V3, V4.1) plus:

- Scan (S): reveals resources within radius, cooldown 15s.
- Jump (J): brief Y-axis displacement, cooldown 2s.
- Attack (A): plasma projectile, cooldown 3s.
- Inventory (I): modal with material counters and craftable recipes.
- Crafting system that deducts materials and applies permanent upgrades (movement speed, passive food, shield, scanner boost, double jump).
- Resource counts shared between HUD and inventory in real time.

